---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---
<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy - BodhicAI">
    
        
        <div>
            <p>Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString()}</p>
            <h3>1. Information We Collect</h3>
            <p>At BodhicAI, we collect minimal personal information to provide our services. This includes your name, email address, and authentication credentials when you sign up. We do not store your raw payment details; all transactions are processed securely by our payment gateway partners (e.g., Razorpay).</p>
            
            <h3>2. Authentication & Third-Party Login</h3>
            <p>If you choose to log in using third-party identity providers (such as GitHub) or direct email authentication, we request access only to your basic profile information, specifically your <strong>email address</strong>, <strong>name</strong>, and <strong>profile picture</strong>. We use this data exclusively to authenticate your identity, create your user account on our platform, and display your avatar/username on your public profile. We will never share or sell your profile data to third parties.</p>

            <h3>3. How We Use Your Information</h3>
            <p>Your information is used solely to provide, maintain, and improve the BodhicAI marketplace. This includes facilitating transactions between buyers and creators, sending transactional emails, and ensuring the security of our platform.</p>
            
            <h3>4. Data Security</h3>
            <p>We implement industry-standard security measures to protect your personal information. Our platform strictly adheres to standard compliance frameworks to prevent unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction of your data.</p>
            
            <h3>5. Contact Us</h3>
            <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or wish to request data deletion, please contact us at <a href="mailto:support@bodhicai.tech?subject=Privacy%20Data%20Request">support@bodhicai.tech</a>.</p>
        </div>
    
</LegalLayout>
